;; oi's known non-passes over its run corpus, by program (bin/oi check; doc/ocaml/OCAML-SURVEY.md, "As built: O5
;; (write-ahead)"): a failing program listed here is reported "fail known REASON (...)", and test/ocaml/divergences.edn's
;; classes match the reason; a listed program that passes is reported stale. Read with the Clojure reader.
;; An entry is [ID TEXT KIND SHA]: KIND a prefix of the run's reason, SHA (kind "status ") a prefix of the output's sha256 the failure was
;; made for: a status reason names no output, so another failure of the same status falls in no class (re-review 030's finding 4).
;; The pin "e3b0c44298fc" is the digest of empty output (asmcomp/optargs, asmcomp/static_catch_unboxing): it accepts any run that prints nothing, whatever
;; its status (these two exit 0 where ocamlc exits 2: check-suite-oi.edn; re-review 042's finding 2, 056's finding 5).
[
 ["statmemprof/moved_while_blocking" "gc: Gc.Memprof's sampling" "timeout "]
 ["statmemprof/thread_exit_in_callback" "gc: Gc.Memprof's sampling" "output differs ("]
 ["misc/darkening_work" "gc: the major collector's work" "output differs ("]
 ["weak-ephe-final/ephetest" "gc: ephemerons emptied by a collection" "output differs ("]
 ["weak-ephe-final/ephetest3" "gc: ephemerons emptied by a collection" "output differs ("]
;; O7 (the suite corpus, bin/oi suite check): the testsuite's programs without a .reference or with modules
]
